.TH SNPRINTF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
snprintf \- format output into a bounded byte buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int snprintf(char* " buffer ", size_t " capacity ", const char* " format ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats output using the same conversions as
.BR fprintf (3crunch):
.BR %d ,
.BR %ld ,
.BR %lld ,
.BR %u ,
.BR %lu ,
.BR %zu ,
.BR %llu ,
.BR %x ,
.BR %lx ,
.BR %llx ,
.BR %f ,
.BR %.17g ,
.BR %Lf ,
.BR %.17Lg ,
.BR %s ,
.BR %c ,
and
.BR %% .
The compiler accepts up to 127 additional numeric or byte-pointer arguments
for this library function.
Extra arguments are evaluated but not used.
.PP
The capacity includes the terminating NUL. For a positive capacity, at most
capacity minus one bytes are stored and a terminating NUL is written, including
after a format error. For zero capacity no bytes are stored and the buffer
may be null. The caller must provide a writable buffer of at least capacity
bytes when capacity is positive. Input strings and the destination must not
overlap.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes that would have been written, excluding the
terminating NUL, even if the output was truncated. Returns \-1 for an invalid
format, missing or incompatible argument, null format or string, unsupported
real value, unrepresentable count, or null buffer with
positive capacity. The last error sets
.B errno
to
.BR EINVAL .
No particular errno is guaranteed for format errors.
.SH NOTES
Literal field widths and the
.B \-
and
.B 0
flags follow
.BR fprintf (3crunch).
Other precisions, dynamic widths and other flags are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fprintf (3crunch)
